+#
+# Correctness of GROUP BY edge._dst over a 1-step GO. With
+# --enable_partial_edge_agg=false this stays Aggregate over ExpandAll.
+# With the flag on, storage returns partial SUM/COUNT/MIN/MAX and graphd
+# merges them. The rows below are the same in both plans. now() is not
+# pushed; a null amount does not add to SUM or COUNT.
+Feature: Partial edge aggregate by dst
+
+  Background:
+    Given an empty graph
+    And create a space with following options:
+      | partition_num  | 3        |
+      | replica_factor | 1        |
+      | vid_type       | INT64    |
+    And having executed:
+      """
+      CREATE TAG person(name string);
+      CREATE EDGE buy(amount int, ts int);
+      """
+    And wait 3 seconds
+    And having executed:
+      """
+      INSERT VERTEX person(name) VALUES 1:("u1"), 2:("u2"), 3:("u3"), 10:("i1"), 11:("i2");
+      INSERT EDGE buy(amount, ts) VALUES 1->10@0:(5, 10), 1->11@0:(7, 10), 1->11@1:(NULL, 10), 2->10@0:(4, 1), 3->11@0:(9, 10);
+      """
+
+  Scenario: sum and count by dst, null amount skipped
+    When executing query:
+      """
+      GO FROM 10, 11 OVER buy REVERSELY WHERE buy.ts > 5
+      YIELD buy._dst AS uid, buy.amount AS amt
+      | GROUP BY $-.uid
+      YIELD $-.uid AS uid, sum($-.amt) AS sales, count($-.amt) AS n
+      """
+    Then the result should be, in any order, with relax comparison:
+      | uid | sales | n |
+      | 1   | 12    | 2 |
+      | 3   | 9     | 1 |
+    When executing query:
+      """
+      GO FROM 10 OVER buy REVERSELY WHERE buy.ts > 5
+      YIELD buy._dst AS uid, buy.amount AS amt
+      | GROUP BY $-.uid
+      YIELD $-.uid AS uid, min($-.amt) AS lo, max($-.amt) AS hi
+      """
+    Then the result should be, in any order, with relax comparison:
+      | uid | lo | hi |
+      | 1   | 5  | 5  |
+
+  Scenario: empty filter result has no group
+    When executing query:
+      """
+      GO FROM 10, 11 OVER buy REVERSELY WHERE buy.ts > 100
+      YIELD buy._dst AS uid, buy.amount AS amt
+      | GROUP BY $-.uid
+      YIELD $-.uid AS uid, sum($-.amt) AS sales
+      """
+    Then the result should be, in any order, with relax comparison:
+      | uid | sales |
